"tomandcatherine" <tomandcatherine@comcast.net> writes:
> If you are throwing daggers, does the strength damage bonus apply to them?
> (For example, if you are strength 25, does every dagger you throw do an
> extra 6 damage?)

Yes.

> The weapons spoiler is a little ambiguous on this point -- it says
> specific things about weapons fired from launchers (arrows, etc.) and
> weapons wielded, but it's not entirely clear on weapons thrown.  It seems
> like the damage bonus should apply, but I can't tell for sure.

It seems clear enough to me.

  Additional damage can occur to all of the above attacks (even against
  shades):
  [...]

  +   The STRENGTH +DAM bonus from the attributes adjustment table
      above.  This won't occur if you aren't allowed the increase
      damage bonus, or if you're firing a missile from a launcher.

Since you're not firing a missile from a launcher, and it's not an
attack that has previously described as not being allowed the increase
damage bonus (mirrors, eggs, cream pies, venom) you get it.

